@0    = ~Ah, you must be <CHARNAME>, Hero of Nashkel! I hope you’ve been enjoying your time in Baldur’s Gate thus far. My benefactor, Zashir Anskuln, would like to invite you to the Dukes’ Retreat Isle. Please speak to Captain Adrik outside the Harbor Master’s Building near the docks when you are ready to embark to the Isle.~
@1    = ~The Dukes’ Retreat? Ooh, <CHARNAME>, I've always wanted to go! Very exclusive. They say the new owner doesn't even live in Baldur's Gate!~
@2    = ~Who is Zashir Anskuln?~
@3    = ~What can you tell me about the Isle?~
@4    = ~Should I bring anything?~
@5    = ~Thank you; I’ll take the invitation now.~
@6    = ~Truthfully, I don’t know. I haven’t met her. She sent a letter to the Messengers’ Guild requesting that someone deliver the invitation to you and several others. I believe that your exploits along the Sword Coast earned you an invitation.~
@7    = ~It used to be owned by a noble by the name of Tyndal Marlow, who sold it when he moved to Waterdeep. It is currently owned by Zashir Anskuln. I understand that Zashir is hoping to continue Tyndal’s tradition of hosting exclusive parties with well-to-do people. I assume that your exploits along the Sword Coast earned you an invitation.~
@8    = ~I can’t say for certain, but I don’t believe that to be necessary. If Zashir’s parties are anything like Tyndal Marlow’s, everything will be both exceptional and accounted for.~
@9    = ~Most excellent. No need to worry about a courier fee; Zashir already accounted for that. Good <DAYNIGHT> to you, my <LADYLORD>.~
